SUMMARY:Deadline: Mozilla Foundation Fellowship 2027-28 (up to USD 125\,000
 \, letter of intent 17 Dec)
DESCRIPTION:Mozilla Foundation's 2027-28 Fellowship backs 10 people working
  on technology that is "too early\, too unexpected\, or too ambitious for 
 anyone else to fund"\, reimagining emerging technology while its future is
  still being decided. Each Fellow receives up to USD 125\,000 over 12 mont
 hs (USD 100\,000 stipend plus USD 25\,000 project budget) to lead an indep
 endent project. Mozilla's fellowship work spans responsible AI\, digital r
 ights\, online privacy and surveillance\, internet freedom\, open source a
 nd data governance\; listed 2027 focus areas include business models for a
  post-agentic web (see the call page for the full list). This replaces the
  nomination-only process of the 2026 cycle with an open letter-of-intent r
 oute. APPLICATION: submit a Letter of Intent by 17 December 2026\, 11:59 P
 M Pacific\; shortlisted applicants are invited to later stages\, which may
  include interviews. The fellowship begins 1 June 2027.\n\nOrganisation: M
 ozilla Foundation\nLocation: International. Fellows lead independent proje
 cts\; the cohort meets at in-person gatherings.\nAward: Up to USD 125\,000
  over 12 months: a USD 100\,000 stipend plus a USD 25\,000 project budget.
  10 Fellowships awarded. No application fee stated.\nDuration: 12 months\,
  from 1 June 2027.\n\nMore: https://www.mozillafoundation.org/en/what-we-d
 o/grantmaking/fellowship/2027-call-for-applications/?utm_source=artificial
 nouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
